<title>SOUTH KOREA: Seoul insurers able to seek overseas reinsurance.</title>
<headline>Seoul insurers able to seek overseas reinsurance.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea will allow domestic fire insurance companies to indemnify foreign reinsurance companies for their risks effective from April 1, the Ministry of Finance and Economy said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>At present Korea Reinsurance Co Ltd monopolised reinsurance trade of local fire insurers.</p>
<p>A ministry statement said the government already lifted the similar bans imposed on other types of insurance companies, including automobile and shipping insurance.</p>
</text>
